## Evaluation Analysis

The Random Forest model achieved extremely high performance
(MAE ≈ 0.00002, R² ≈ 0.99999).

This indicates a strong predictive relationship between selected
features and cost. However, such near-perfect performance may
suggest the presence of highly correlated proxy variables or
deterministic cost drivers in the dataset.

Further validation on unseen real-world data is required to
confirm generalization performance.
